* Const component reference -- the "## Example" netlist verbatim.
* No title line: general-mna's build_system parses this as a SPICE *fragment*, not a document --
* the first line is a real element/block, not a skipped title. A leading title line would parse
* as a bogus device declaration instead.
*
* SETPOINT is the scalar form (value=<f64>); OFFSETS the vector form (value=[x,y,z], a Python
* list literal). Both are time-invariant, so every row must repeat the same values:
* SETPOINT = 5, OFFSETS = [1, 2, 3] (see test_const.py::test_example_scalar_and_vector_constants).
SETPOINT kind=const value=5
OFFSETS kind=const value=[1,2,3]
